        "problem": "$\\frac{5{b}^{2}}{2}÷\\frac{b}{7}=$",
        "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\frac{5{b}^{2}}{2}÷\\frac{b}{7},\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5{b}^{2}}{2}÷\\frac{b}{7} & = \\\\ \\frac{5{b}^{2}}{2}\\cdot \\frac{7}{b} & = \\\\ \\frac{35{b}^{2}}{2b} & = \\\\ \\frac{35{b}^{\\cancel{2}}}{2\\cancel{b}} & = \\\\ \\frac{35b}{2} & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the final step, we canceled out a common factor of $b$ in the numerator and denominator.",
