        "problem": "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{13{x}^{2}-19x-16}{(3x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A,$ $B$ and $C$ are real constants, calculate $A+B+C.$",
        "worked_solution": "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{13{x}^{2}-19x-16}{(3x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}=\\frac{A}{(3x+2)}+\\frac{B}{(x-3)}+\\frac{C}{(x+1)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(3x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ gives\n\n$$\n13{x}^{2}-19x-16=A(x-3)(x+1)+B(3x+2)(x+1)+C(3x+2)(x-3).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{2}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}-19(-\\frac{2}{3})-16 & =A(-\\frac{2}{3}-3)(-\\frac{2}{3}+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+2)(-\\frac{2}{3}+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(-\\frac{2}{3})+1)(-\\frac{2}{3}-3) \\\\ \\frac{52}{9}+\\frac{38}{3}-16 & =A(\\frac{(-11)(1)}{9}) \\\\ \\frac{52+114-144}{9} & =A(-\\frac{11}{9}) \\\\ A & =-\\frac{22}{11} \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13(3)^{2}-19(3)-16 & =A(3-3)(3+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(3)+2)(3+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(3)+2)(3-3) \\\\ 117-57-16 & =B(44) \\\\ B & =\\frac{44}{44} \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}13(-1)^{2}-19(-1)-16 & =A(-1-3)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(3(-1)+2)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+C(3(-1)+2)(-1-3) \\\\ 13+19-16 & =C(4) \\\\ C & =\\frac{16}{4} \\\\ C & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B+C & =(-2)+1+4=3.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
