        "knowledge_point": "Matching a Single Coefficient",
        "problem": "The following equation is true for all values of $x.$\n\n$$\n-5{x}^{2}+mx-6=-5{x}^{2}-3x-6\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of the constant $m?$",
        "worked_solution": "Since the equation is true for all values of $x,$ the expressions on both sides must be exactly the same. That means the coefficients of the matching powers of $x$ must be equal.\n\nWe compare the linear terms on both sides. On the left-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $m.$ On the right-hand side, the coefficient of $x$ is $-3.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nm=-3.\n$$",
